.Dd November 5, 2026
.Dt IF_EVENTLOG 4
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm if_eventlog
.Nd network interface eventlog provider
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the kernel-side producer for the
.Dq if
.Xr eventlog 9
provider.
It streams every observable change to network interface state
\(em attach, detach, rename, link state, configuration changes,
and address add/remove
\(em as schema-driven binary records, plus optional periodic
per-interface counter samples, split by transport protocol.
.Pp
A single eventlog session is created per virtual network stack
.Xr ( vimage 9 ) ;
events scope naturally to the subscriber's view of the network
stack.
The provider's per-event keyword filters let consumers subscribe
selectively, for example
.Dq SAMPLE only
to receive only the periodic counter samples without the
configuration noise.
.Sh KEYWORDS
The provider exposes the following keywords for subscription
filtering.
.Bl -tag -width "SAMPLE_PACKETS"
.It META
Session-level metadata
.Pq Vt IF_INFO .
.It SAMPLE
Periodic per-interface byte samples
.Pq Vt IF_SAMPLE_BYTES .
.It SAMPLE_PACKETS
Periodic per-interface packet samples
.Pq Vt IF_SAMPLE_PACKETS .
.It LIFECYCLE
Interface attach, detach, and rename
.Pq Vt IF_ATTACH , Vt IF_DETACH , Vt IF_RENAME .
.It LINK
Link-state transitions
.Pq Vt IF_LINK_STATE .
.It CONFIG
Administrative flag, MTU, and capability changes
.Pq Vt IF_FLAGS_CHANGE , Vt IF_MTU_CHANGE , Vt IF_CAPABILITIES_CHANGE .
.It ADDR
Interface address add and remove
.Pq Vt IF_ADDR_ADD , Vt IF_ADDR_REMOVE .
.El
.Sh EVENTS
.Bl -tag -width "IF_CAPABILITIES_CHANGE"
.It IF_INFO
Session-level metadata: the configured sample period in
microseconds (zero if no sampler is currently armed), the VNET
identifier, and the count of attached ifnets at session-create
time.
Emitted once per session and replayed via
.Fn dump_state .
.It IF_ATTACH
An ifnet has just been added to the global table.
Carries the interface index, name, link-layer type
.Pq Dv IFT_* ,
driver name, MTU, baud rate, and the link-layer hardware
address.
This is the only point at which the
.Pq ifindex No \(-> Em name
binding consumers maintain is established for that ifindex.
.Pp
The live event fires from within
.Xr if_attach 9 ,
before the driver writes the hardware address, so
.Va hwaddr
may be empty for a freshly attached interface; the authoritative
value arrives with the
.Fn dump_state
replay a subscriber receives on attach and, on any later link-layer
address change
.Pq Xr if_setlladdr 9 ,
a re-emitted
.Vt IF_ATTACH .
Interfaces with no link-layer address, such as
.Xr lo 4 ,
report an empty
.Va hwaddr
by design.
.It IF_DETACH
An ifnet has been removed from the global table.
After this event the kernel may reuse the ifindex for a future
.Vt IF_ATTACH .
.It IF_RENAME
An ifnet's user-visible name has changed; the ifindex is
unchanged.
Consumers update their
.Pq ifindex No \(-> Em name
table on this event.
.It IF_LINK_STATE
The interface's link state has transitioned.
The new state is one of
.Dv UNKNOWN ,
.Dv DOWN ,
or
.Dv UP ;
the previous state can be inferred from the consumer's running
table or from the most recent
.Vt IF_LINK_STATE
or
.Vt IF_ATTACH
event.
.It IF_FLAGS_CHANGE , IF_MTU_CHANGE , IF_CAPABILITIES_CHANGE
A
.Dv SIOCSIFFLAGS ,
.Dv SIOCSIFMTU ,
or
.Dv SIOCSIFCAP /
.Dv SIOCSIFCAPNV
operation has just completed.
Both the old and new values are reported.
.It IF_ADDR_ADD , IF_ADDR_REMOVE
A network-layer address has been added to or removed from an
interface.
.It IF_SAMPLE
.Sy Deprecated ;
no longer emitted.
Superseded by
.Vt IF_SAMPLE_BYTES
and
.Vt IF_SAMPLE_PACKETS ,
which split bytes and packets by transport protocol instead of
reporting flat totals.
The struct and event definitions are retained only so older
captures still decode.
.It IF_SAMPLE_BYTES , IF_SAMPLE_PACKETS
Periodic per-interface counter samples emitted with period
.Va kern.eventlog.if.sample_period_us
microseconds when at least one subscriber is attached.
.Vt IF_SAMPLE_BYTES
carries in/out byte totals plus a TCP/UDP/other split of each and is
selected by the
.Sy SAMPLE
keyword;
.Vt IF_SAMPLE_PACKETS
carries in/out packet totals plus the same split, along with the
errors/drops/multicast/noproto counters carried over from the
deprecated
.Vt IF_SAMPLE ,
and is selected by
.Sy SAMPLE_PACKETS .
The
.Sy other
counters cover every non-TCP/UDP IP packet
.Pq e.g. ICMP ,
classified at the same IP-dispatch site as the TCP/UDP counters, so
tcp+udp+other is internally consistent for that split.
The L2 in/out totals in the same sample are driver/stack counters and
are not guaranteed to equal tcp+udp+other: non-IP L2 traffic, TSO/LRO,
IPv4 reassembly, locally forwarded traffic, and multi-port
.Pq Xr lagg 4
interfaces (where L2 sums member-port driver counters asynchronously,
and protocol counts accrue on the aggregate ifp) all diverge.
On lagg member ports the protocol split is usually near zero while L2
totals reflect wire traffic.
Do not derive
.Sy other
as total minus tcp minus udp.
The sampler is gated by the
.Sy subscribers_changed
callback and costs nothing while no consumer is listening.
.El
.Sh SYSCTLS
The provider's per-keyword filtering and default state are
exposed as standard
.Xr eventlog 9
sysctls under
.Va kern.eventlog.if .
The
.Nm
producer adds one provider-specific tunable:
.Bl -tag -width "kern.eventlog.if.sample_period_us"
.It Va kern.eventlog.if.sample_period_us
Period between
.Vt IF_SAMPLE_BYTES
and
.Vt IF_SAMPLE_PACKETS
emissions, in microseconds, in the range
.Bq Em 1000 , 1800000000
(1 ms to 30 min).
Default
.Em 500000
(2 Hz).
The sampler is armed only while the provider has subscribers,
so changing this knob has no effect when no consumer is
attached.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ifconfig 8 ,
.Xr ifnet 9 ,
.Xr eventlog 9 ,
.Xr vimage 9 ,
.Xr elog 1
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
provider first appeared in
.Fx 15.0 .
